WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.912
YieldShield on Monad gives crypto holders two ways to exit. Withdraw the
remaining deposited asset,

00:00:05.912 --> 00:00:11.823
or surrender the position for its eligible backing payout. Another
participant supplies first-loss capital and

00:00:11.823 --> 00:00:17.735
earns a share of realized gains. This narrated overview shows the
deployed testnet product and

00:00:17.735 --> 00:00:19.312
its recorded transaction evidence.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:25.672
Five funded pools are deployed on Monad testnet. The reference markets
support wrapped native MON

00:00:25.672 --> 00:00:31.544
and shMON, backed by either Test USD or redeemable test-vault shares.
RedStone supplies MON pricing

00:00:31.544 --> 00:00:37.417
directly on chain. Test USD has no monetary value and is not Circle
USDC. Each

00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:40.548
pool began with fifty thousand test backing units.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.969
The protection form exposes the asset, backing and gain-sharing fees
before signing. There is no

00:00:46.969 --> 00:00:52.937
recurring premium. A backing exit requires a sixty-second testnet wait
and surrenders the remaining asset.

00:00:52.937 --> 00:00:58.906
Dynamic email authentication and embedded wallets are integrated. Their
user signing walkthrough is still being

00:00:58.906 --> 00:01:02.885
verified; this video does not present a live wallet transaction.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:09.161
The separate scenario lab makes gains and losses understandable without
pretending a formula is a

00:01:09.161 --> 00:01:14.972
market price. Holders can compare taking the remaining asset with using
the capped backing option.

00:01:14.972 --> 00:01:20.783
Junior providers accept first losses. Their one-hundred-and-twenty-
second withdrawal notice does not release capital that is

00:01:20.783 --> 00:01:22.333
still committed to protection.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:28.711
Test assets let visitors obtain demonstration tokens, wrap native MON
and stake through the actual

00:01:28.711 --> 00:01:34.623
shMonad integration. The test vault uses deposited backing and
deliberately funded test yield. Its payout

00:01:34.623 --> 00:01:40.534
is in vault shares, followed by a separate redemption. shMON uses
conservative withdrawal value; staking

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:44.081
does not mean that an unstake queue has completed.

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:50.861
The status page reads verified contracts and fresh prices through a
read-only API. MON reference

00:01:50.861 --> 00:01:57.173
rounds older than one hundred and twenty seconds are rejected. Scenario
prices remain isolated. The

00:01:57.173 --> 00:02:03.484
API has no wallet signing key. Users keep explicit transaction
confirmations, exact token approvals and

00:02:03.484 --> 00:02:05.588
account, network and contract checks.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:12.601
Both internal transaction suites completed with canonical receipts and
received-token balance checks. They cover deposits,

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:19.153
both holder exits, provider claims and actual withdrawal waits. One
failed gas estimate and its

00:02:19.153 --> 00:02:25.704
successful reviewed retry remain visible. YieldShield predates
Metropolis; the protocol foundation is reused and disclosed.

00:02:25.704 --> 00:02:32.255
The Monad app, integrations and deployment form the new milestone. No
adoption or independent audit

00:02:32.255 --> 00:02:33.129
is claimed.
